# Reproduction for the two accent bugs on the detail window and the popup.
# The dark accent is chosen BEFORE the 1:00 timer is made, because every
# emu button press costs a couple of seconds: doing settings first keeps the
# 60 s drain unambiguously inside the two waits below. Run with -t none, so
# the harness's clock pinning does not disturb the countdown.
#
# Before the fix: the digits sat white on the exposed light grey once the
# water block drained below them, and the popup title sat black on the dark
# accent. Now the text sits on an opaque accent plate and inks white.

note back out of the duration picker to set the accent first
wait 4              # the app's first window needs to be up before presses land
press back          # menu (empty, just the + and cog rows)
press down          # to the cog row
press select        # Settings
press down 4        # to the Accent Color row
press select        # the colour picker, opening on Malachite
press down 3        # Dark Candy Apple Red
press select        # applies and pops back to settings
press back          # menu, cursor on the cog row
press up            # to the + row

note now make a 1:00 timer and start it
press select        # duration picker
press select        # off hours
press up 1          # one minute
press select        # off minutes
press select        # confirm -- detail opens, paused, water full
press select        # start the timer

note wait for the water to drain below the digits band
wait 40             # ~40 s of the 60: line sits well under the digits
shot digits-over-grey

note wait out the rest of the minute; popup auto-closes after 15 s
wait 25             # expires at ~60 s, popup up from 10 s before this shot
shot time-up
